cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EasyClassifier in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "EasyClassifier: Machine Learning without Programming"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hassanat
    given-names: Ahmad B. A.
    email: ahmad.hassanat@gmail.com
version: 0.8.1
date-released: 2026-09-28
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ahmadhassant/easyclassifier"
url: "https://github.com/ahmadhassant/easyclassifier"
abstract: >-
  EasyClassifier is a guided, menu-driven tool that lets researchers without
  programming experience build and evaluate classification models from a CSV
  or Excel file. It enforces leakage-free preprocessing, reports an honest
  final score for the selected classifier (final test set or nested
  cross-validation), checks the chosen class column, uses default parameters
  for reproducibility, and writes a plain-language report with a
  ready-to-adapt methods paragraph.
keywords:
  - machine learning
  - classification
  - no-code
  - reproducibility
  - k-nearest neighbours
  - Hassanat distance
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Dimensionality Invariant Similarity Measure"
    authors:
      - family-names: Hassanat
        given-names: Ahmad B.
    journal: "Journal of American Science"
    volume: 10
    issue: 8
    year: 2014
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "arXiv:1409.0923"
